  "id": "Compound::DB00499 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Flutamide, a well-known androgen receptor antagonist, is linked to Cyp2c19 through a series of biological pathways that involve both direct and indirect mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Flutamide, as part of the Androgen Receptor Antagonists class, binds to Cyp2c19 through the interaction with Bicalutamide or Nilutamide, which are also members of this class. This indicates a potential shared mechanism of action involving the targeting of Cyp2c19, possibly through a common structural feature such as the (Trifluoromethyl)Benzenes group. The presence of multiple pathways that ultimately lead to Cyp2c19 binding highlights a possible role in drug metabolism or enzyme induction, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Cyp2c19 in the metabolic processing of androgen receptor antagonists, suggesting a broader pharmacological significance in the context of drug-target interactions.",
